      "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
      "source": "pdf_layout",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "In this paper we introduce the differential meet-in-the- middle framework, a new cryptanalysis technique for symmetric prim- itives. Our new cryptanalysis method combines techniques from both meet-in-the-middle and differential cryptanalysis. As such, the intro- duced technique can be seen as a way of extending meet-in-the-middle attacks and their variants but also as a new way to perform the key recovery part in differential attacks. We apply our approach to SKINNY-128-384 in the single-key model and to AES-256 in the related- key model. Our attack on SKINNY-128-384 permits to break 25 out of the 56 rounds of this variant and improves by two rounds the previous bestknownattacks.ForAES-256weattack12roundsbyconsideringtwo relatedkeys,thusoutperformingthepreviousbestrelated-keyattackon AES-256 with only two related keys by 2 rounds. ·",
      "extractor": "pdfplumber_section_boundary"
    },
